  "response": "**Setting up with Bayes' theorem:**\n\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002, so P(no D) = 0.998\n- Sensitivity: P(+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(–|no D) = 0.95, so P(+|no D) = 0.05\n\n**P(+) = P(+|D)P(D) + P(+|no D)P(no D)**\n= (0.98)(0.002) + (0.05)(0.998)\n= 0.00196 + 0.04990\n= 0.05186\n\n**P(D|+) = P(+|D)P(D) / P(+)**\n= 0.00196 / 0.05186\n= 0.0377858...\n≈ **3.78%**\n\n**Sanity check** with a population of 500,000:\n- Diseased: 1,000 → true positives = 980\n- Not diseased: 499,000 → false positives = 0.05 × 499,000 = 24,950\n- Total positives = 980 + 24,950 = 25,930\n- P(disease | positive) = 980 / 25,930 = 0.037795 ≈ 3.78%\n\nBoth methods agree.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
